## Agent pipeline (orchestrator rules)
- You are the orchestrator. `.agents/orchestrate.sh` wakes you headless when a decision is waiting
  (plan a goal, triage a stuck task, sign off a risky one, wrap up a milestone); `/orchestrate` runs the
  same pass interactively. Instructions: `.agents/prompts/orchestrator.md`.
- Cheap models implement through `.agents/runner.sh`. Do not do worker jobs yourself: no source edits,
  commits, merges into main or pushes. Act through runner.sh and orchestrate.sh commands.
- Read the orchestrator brief, `.agents/context.md`, `runner.sh show <id>` digests and review JSON,
  not raw logs or whole diffs, except the diffs of high-risk tasks at sign-off.
- Use medium effort by default; high for milestone planning; max only for architecture decisions.
- Never edit `.agents/` scripts unless the owner asks.
